Package: *
Pin: release o=DANOS
Pin-Priority: 1000

# frr carries the DANOS zebra NHG patch (0001-zebra-nhg-...-10.3.patch, see
# toolkit/frr-patches/). The overlay is a second DANOS source served during the
# build, and its Release has no Origin/Archive that the blanket o=DANOS pin above
# could match, so the patched build only won by version number. That is fragile:
# a Debian security upload (e.g. 10.3-3+deb13u2) sorts higher than
# 10.3-3+deb13u1danos1 and would silently drop the patch. Pin frr to the overlay
# by archive name so the patch survives Debian point updates.
#
# Scoped to frr on purpose: pinning the whole overlay would also freeze the
# Debian-forced packages in it and stop security updates there.
Package: frr frr-snmp frr-pythontools
Pin: release a=danos-local-overlay
Pin-Priority: 1001

# iputils is no longer forked. The pin here used to hold ping at DANOS's 2018
# build for a local -Z option ("source from this interface's address"), which
# the op-mode ping wrapper needed for loopback interfaces. The wrapper now
# resolves the loopback address itself and passes it to the standard -I, so
# Debian's current iputils is used unmodified.
#
# grub/shim are sourced from stock Debian 13 for the trixie build, not DANOS's
# own repo (DANOS no longer builds these packages), so no forced-pin needed.
